0. PURPOSE

Dorkroom is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
(the "AGPLv3"), a copy of which is distributed in the file LICENSE.

Dorkroom is also distributed as a native mobile application. The operators of
mobile application stores require, as a condition of distribution, that end
users accept terms of service which restrict the exercise of rights the AGPLv3
grants: limits on the number of devices an application may be installed on,
and digital rights management applied to the delivered binary, among others.
Those restrictions are imposed by the store operator, not by us, but their
presence would otherwise make it impossible to distribute Dorkroom through
such a store while satisfying the AGPLv3.

This exception removes that obstacle. It does not weaken the copyleft. The
obligation to make Corresponding Source available is untouched, and is
restated in section 3 below.


1. DEFINITIONS

The terms "Program", "covered work", "convey", "modify", "object code",
"Corresponding Source", "User Product", and "Installation Information" carry
the meanings given to them in the AGPLv3.

A "Managed Distribution Platform" is a service that distributes application
software to end users and that conditions such distribution on the end user's
acceptance of terms of service imposed by the operator of that service. Apple's
App Store, Google Play, and Microsoft Store are Managed Distribution Platforms.


