5. NOTICES IN SOURCE FILES

Section 7 of the AGPLv3 requires that terms added under it be accompanied, in
the relevant source files, by either a statement of those terms or a notice
indicating where to find them, and states that this requirement applies to
permissive and non-permissive terms alike.

A notice pointing to this document is carried at the entry point of each
covered work in this repository:

  apps/mobile/index.js            the iOS application
  apps/dorkroom/src/main.tsx      the web application
  packages/logic/src/index.ts     shared logic, embedded in the iOS app
  packages/ui/src/index.ts        shared web components

Those notices point here; this document states the terms. Adding a new
top-level application or package to the repository means carrying the same
notice at its entry point.

The package at packages/api/ carries no such notice, and deliberately so: it is
released under the MIT license rather than the AGPLv3, so this exception has
nothing to add to it. See packages/api/LICENSE.


